# Torches: one coal (or one charcoal) and one stick give four (26.3 recipe
# data, a 1x2 recipe, so no table is needed).
#
# Depth 4: get_torch -> get_coal -> get_wooden_pickaxe -> get_planks (a leaf).
# `get_coal` is the only deep child; the sticks are one frame, and the craft
# itself is a primitive.
#
# Why the rules are ordered this way: the goal check is on top, and the default
# is four because one craft yields exactly four. The coal rule and the stick
# rule come before the craft, so `craft(torch)` never fails
# `missing_ingredients`: a failed `get_coal` makes its rule ineligible for one
# tick and the stick rule gets its turn, instead of the skill failing on the
# first tick. Charcoal counts as the coal key here (the 26.3 recipe accepts
# both), and `get_coal` is only called when neither is held, so a body that
# already has charcoal mines nothing new. The last rule is the craft itself;
# it fires again while the count is short, which is how a goal of eight or
# twelve torches gets two or three crafts.
skill get_torch(n: int = 4)
  doc "Have n torches, crafted four at a time from coal or charcoal and a stick."
  rules:
    count(torch) >= $n -> done
    count(coal) < 1 and count(charcoal) < 1 -> do get_coal(1)
    count(stick) < 1 -> do get_sticks(1)
    true -> craft(torch)
